                <pb facs="0702" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg584"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">312.1722 Sandino/3½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-01T12:00:00-06:00">March 1,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Your 33, February 25, 2 p.m. At interviews had with the President and the
                    Acting Secretary of State I communicated to them the substance of your telegram
                    and both expressed satisfaction and appeared to agree with your views. It is my
                    belief that if Sandino continues to be of the same mind with regard to seeking
                    asylum in Mexico, the matter may be expected to proceed along the lines
                    indicated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
